<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0017/e_0002/normalization> <http://digistrucmed.org/normalizationMappingStatus> "UNMAPPED" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/StrengthEntity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0017/tu_0010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Long-term treatment with an antiplatelet agent, generally aspirin in doses of 75 to 81 mg, is recommended for patients with HF due to ischemic cardiomyopathy, whether or not they are receiving ACE inhibitors. (Strength of Evidence = B) Warfarin (goal INR 2.0-3.0) and clopidogrel (75 mg) also have prevented vascular events in post-MI patients and may be considered as alternatives to aspirin. (Strength of Evidence = B)" .
