<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0017/tu_0004> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "It is recommended that the dose of digoxin, which should be based on lean body mass, renal function, and concomitant medications, should be 0.125 mg daily in the majority of patients and the serum digoxin level should be < 1.0 ng/mL, generally 0.7-0.9 ng/mL. (Strength of Evidence = B)" .
